The staff's deficiency letter arising from examination 2011-0447 is enclose=
d. It describes five deficiencies, all of them within the advertising and p=
erformance presentation scope of this examination.<br />
<br />
The most significant is the growth composite. Between January 2009 and Sept=
ember 2010 the composite excluded four terminated accounts whose performanc=
e was below the composite median, and the pitchbook presented the resulting=
 returns without disclosing the exclusions or the composite's construction.=
 The firm's written advertising review procedure was not followed for eleve=
n of the nineteen pieces in our sample, and three pieces present net return=
s derived from a fee schedule lower than the schedule actually charged to t=
he accounts in the composite.<br />
<br />
The staff reviewed the firm's billing arrangements only to the extent neces=
sary to test the net return calculation. The firm bills by invoice and repo=
rted no custody. Nothing in this letter concerns Rule 206(4)-2 and the staf=
f makes no finding on that subject.<br />
<br />
Please respond in writing within thirty days describing the corrective acti=
on the firm will take on each item.<br />
